PDB  
;The minor form (current entry) of the recombinant cytotoxin-1, present in aqueous solution due to cis-trans isomerism of Val7-Pro8 peptide bond. The isomer with trans form of this bond is attributed to major form of the toxin (entry 5T8A).
;
5T8A  unspecified 
PDB  
;The recombinant cytotoxin-1 (this toxin) features an additional Met-residue at the N-terminus, compared to the native protein (entry 1RL5).
;
1RL5  unspecified 
BMRB 'Minor form of the recombinant cytotoxin-1 from N. oxiana' 34039 unspecified 
